{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEightAnnihilation"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.ajHomElement_annihilates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.ajHomElement_annihilates","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L177-L197","doc":"**The GGM/AJ operator annihilates the 4₁ colored-Jones tower as a torus\nelement (sorry-free) — the concrete content of `aj_mem`.**  The homogenised\norder-3 element `ajHomElement` sends the tower `J41` to `0` at every colour:\n`act3 ajHomElement J41 (M) = 0`.\n\nProof: `act3 Â_hom J = b(N+1)·(P_FE·J)(N) − b(N)·(P_FE·J)(N+1)` and each\n`(P_FE·J)` is the corpus `feRhs` (`annih`), so the two `feRhs` products\ncancel.  This is `Â_hom ∈ { P | P·J = 0 }` at the function-model level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.ajHomElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.ajHomElement","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L170-L175","doc":"**The homogenised order-3 AJ operator as a torus element.**  `Â_hom =\nc₀ + c₁L + c₂L² + c₃L³ ∈ QuantumTorus (ℤ→K)` — the order-raised\nhomogenisation `(L − ρ)·P_FE` of the corpus inhomogeneous operator, with `ρ`\nthe shift ratio `b(N+1)/b(N)` cleared into the coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.hc3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.hc3","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L168-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.hc2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.hc2","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L167-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.hc1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.hc1","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L166-L166","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.hc0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.hc0","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L164-L165","doc":"The order-3 homogeneous coefficients `c₀,c₁,c₂,c₃` of `Â_hom = (L − ρ)·P_FE`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.act2_ggmElement_inhom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.act2_ggmElement_inhom","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L146-L160","doc":"**Residence (honest, `= feRhs`).**  The order-2 torus element carrying the\nfigure-eight coefficients acts on the tower `J41` as the corpus *inhomogeneous*\noperator — its value at colour `M` is `feRhs(q,q^M)`, **not** `0`.  So this\n`ggmElement` is co-resident with the C1 kernel in `QuantumTorus (ℤ→K)`, but it\nis *not* in the strict annihilator ideal; the homogenisation below is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.annih","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.annih","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L132-L142","doc":"**The corpus annihilation as a flat 3-term identity** (unfolding the summed\n`figureEightOperator_annihilates`): at every colour `n`,\n`feCoeff 0·J(n) + feCoeff 1·J(n+1) + feCoeff 2·J(n+2) = feRhs(q,q^n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.act3_homElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.act3_homElement","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L122-L128","doc":"The order-3 element acts as the order-3 difference operator\n`c₀ N·J N + c₁ N·J(N+1) + c₂ N·J(N+2) + c₃ N·J(N+3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.homElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.homElement","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L117-L120","doc":"**The order-3 homogeneous torus element** `c₀ + c₁L + c₂L² + c₃L³` in the\nsame `QuantumTorus (ℤ → K)` as `ggmElement`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.act3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.act3","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L108-L115","doc":"**The order-≤3 function-model action.**  A torus element `f` acts on a colour\ntower `J : ℤ → K` as the q-difference operator whose `L^j`-coefficient is the\ndiagonal `coeffAt f j` (`j = 0,1,2,3`).  For an element supported in degrees\n`{0,1,2,3}` this is its full action; it extends `QuantumTorusAJ.act2` by one\nshift, exactly as the homogenisation `(L − ρ)·P_FE` raises the order by one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.bFn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.bFn","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L103-L104","doc":"The inhomogeneous right-hand side as a ℤ→K function: `b(N) = feRhs(q,q^N)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.aFn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.aFn","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L99-L101","doc":"The `j`-th figure-eight coefficient as a ℤ→K function of the torus degree:\n`aⱼ(N) = feCoeff j q (q^N)` at nonnegative `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.J41","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation.J41","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJTorusAnnihilation.lean#L95-L97","doc":"The colored-Jones tower of `4₁` as a ℤ-indexed function (torus degree),\nagreeing with `coloredJones41 q` at nonnegative colours. ","signatureChunk":0}]}